  "result": "I fixed the option order in `--help`, and the test suite still passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nThe bug was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`. It sorted an option's names by prefix length in reverse, so the long form came first (`--verbose, -v`). I removed `reverse=True`, so short options now come first (`-v, --verbose`). That is the usual click ordering.\n\nNo existing test covers this ordering, and I didn't add one.\n\nThe \"Positional arguments\" section appears before \"Options\". I left that alone because `tests/test_arguments.py` checks for it explicitly.\n\nIf the order you saw was something else, such as the order of the options themselves, tell me what it looked like and I'll look again.",
